Aim:
To write a Java program to demonstrate multilevel inheritance.

Algorithm:
1. Create a class Animal.
2. Create a class Dog that extends Animal.
3. Create a class Puppy that extends Dog.
4. Create an object of Puppy.
5. Call the methods of all three classes.

Program:
import java.util.Scanner;

class Animal {
    void eat() {
        System.out.println("Animal is eating");
    }
}

class Dog extends Animal {
    void bark() {
        System.out.println("Dog is barking");
    }
}

class Puppy extends Dog {
    void weep() {
        System.out.println("Puppy is weeping");
    }
}

public class MultilevelInheritance {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Puppy p = new Puppy();
        p.eat();
        p.bark();
        p.weep();
    }
}



Output:
Animal is eating
Dog is barking
Puppy is weeping


Result:
Thus, multilevel inheritance was demonstrated successfully.
